<title>ITALY: Italy's Ceramiche Ricchetti doubles profits.</title>
<headline>Italy's Ceramiche Ricchetti doubles profits.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated, preliminary)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			  9.0  vs   4.2</p>
<p>    Operating margin			21.0  vs  16.1</p>
<p>    Cons turnover			  251.5  vs 274.4</p>
<p>    Cons net debt			   51.8  vs  81.3</p>
<p>Note - Ceramiche Ricchetti said its operating margin grew mainly due to production rationalisation in Finland and Sweden.</p>
<p>&quot;With a return on equity of 10 percent and a debt/equity ratio of 0.58 percent I believe we can be considered a particularly welcome subject to the capital markets,&quot; said Renzo Arletti, chairman and managing director.</p>
<p>Ceramiche Ricchetti said it registered a good start to orders and sales in the first part of 1997 with January figures &quot;up 10 percent on the previous year, allowing the management to look with optimism at a year in which it expects a further improvement in total profitability.&quot;</p>
<p>--Milan newsroom +392 66129450</p>
</text>
